  (modified versions 2.0.1, 2.0.2).
  Licence: GNU General Public License, version 3.

- PAML 4.10 (https://github.com/abacus-gene/paml): yn00.c and the routines of tools.c it uses.
  Copyright, 1998, Ziheng Yang.
  Licence: GNU General Public License, version 3.

src/coal/kaks_comeron.cpp (the method "Comeron") and src/coal/kaks_li.cpp (the method "Li") are derived from:

- libsequence, as the R package orthologr compiles it into its function gestimator() (orthologr 0.4.3,
  https://github.com/drostlab/orthologr, src/: Comeron95.h, Sites.h, RedundancyCom95.h, SingleSub.h, TwoSubs.h,
  ThreeSubs.h, GranthamWeights.h, Grantham.h, Kimura80.h, Comparisons.h, Sequence.h, gestimator.cpp; libsequence
  itself: https://github.com/molpopgen/libsequence). In src/coal/kaks_comeron.cpp.
  Copyright (C) 2003-2009 Kevin Thornton.
  Licence, as each of those files says: "libsequence is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
  under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either
  version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version."
  Each file also says: "Modified by Sarah Scharfenberg and Hajk-Georg Drost 2014 to work in orthologr without
  using external libraries from libsequence. All changes are also free under the terms of GNU General Public
  License version 2 of the License, or any later version."
  Comeron JM (1995) J Mol Evol 41:1152-1159.

- seqinr 4.2-44 (R package, https://cran.r-project.org/package=seqinr, https://github.com/lbbe-software/seqinr):
  src/kaks.c (the functions kaks, num, fastlwl, catsite, transf, titv1, titv2, titv3, prefastlwl). In src/coal/kaks_li.cpp.
  kaks.c has no copyright notice of its own. Authors of seqinr (its DESCRIPTION): Delphine Charif [aut], Olivier
